  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing the protection, living conditions, and reducing the vulnerabilities of IDPs and host communities among the flood-affected populations in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide shelter/non-food items, water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH), health, early recovery as well as camp coordination and camp management (CCCM) assistance to vulnerable communities affected by flooding in Nigeria. This IOM project provides shelter kits, ensures access to safe water and sanitation facilities, distributes WASH kits and messaging, provides mental health and psychosocial support services, distributes cash assistance, and rehabilitates displacement sites, among other activities. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 8,100 people in the Shelter and Non-Food Items sector, 109,000 people in the WASH sector, 14,780 people in the Health sector, 15,720 people in the Early Recovery sector, and 12,200 people in the CCCM sector.</narrative>
  </description>
